+> `TRAKT_CLIENT_ID` and `SIMKL_CLIENT_ID` are NOT in that payload. It reports
+> `hasTrakt` and `hasSimkl` instead, because both APIs accept a client id alone
+> for public endpoints, so an id read straight off an unauthenticated endpoint
+> lets somebody else's traffic count against your application's rate limit.
+>
+> This reduces how easily an id is collected; it does not make one confidential.
+> A client id is public by design and still appears in the authorization URL the
+> browser opens for the redirect flow. `TRAKT_CLIENT_SECRET`, `SIMKL_CLIENT_SECRET`
+> and `SIMKL_V2_CLIENT_SECRET` are what must stay private, and are never published.
 
